course: dictionary
lesson: 3969
title: The future
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Future is a word with more than one job. As a noun, the future is the time that has not happened yet, everything that comes after now. «Not getting a part or not being picked once does not decide the future; there are other roles, and practice and time change a lot.» Here, the future means all the time still to come in a person's life.
explain: As an adjective, future goes before a noun and describes something that will happen or exist later: future plans, a future king. Look at the word after it. If it names a thing, like «plans» or «king», then future is probably describing that thing.
explain: Future also appears in grammar. In «I will go», the verb shows what is going to happen. Clues like «in the future», «the near future» and «future plans» tell you the word is about time still to come. Put your meaning into the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Future means the time that has not happened yet, what will happen after now.
fact: Your future is what will happen to you later in your life, like your job or your plans.
fact: As an adjective, future describes things that will happen or exist later, like «future jobs».
fact: In school, the future is on the right of a timeline: the past is on the left and the present is in the middle.
fact: «In future» (UK) means from now on, and «the near future» means the time very soon to come.
exercise: «Climate change harms both people and nature, including people in the future.» What does the future mean here? | A map of the world | Times that have already passed | *Times that have not happened yet | A kind of weather
exercise: Maya's teacher says, «We will plan our future projects on Friday.» What does future mean in «future projects»? | Projects about dinosaurs | *Projects that will happen later | Projects finished last year | Projects that are very loud
exercise: In «I will go tomorrow», which word shows the future tense? | go | tomorrow | *will | I
test: «In future, please walk to school.» What does «in future» mean? | *From now on | Long ago | Inside a cupboard | Very slowly
test: In «a future king», what does future tell us about the king? | That he is sad | That he is very old | *That he will be king later | That he lives in a palace
exam: The phrase «the near future» means | The middle of a timeline | *The time very soon to come | A kind of bus | Long ago
